## WHAT YOU CAN DO (no approval needed)

1. **Add blog posts:** Create a new `.md` file in `src/content/blog/`
2. **Edit blog posts:** Modify existing `.md` files in `src/content/blog/`
3. **Edit text content:** Change text in existing `.astro` page files (typos, wording, facts)
4. **Add redirects:** Add new entries to `public/_redirects`

## WHAT YOU CANNOT DO (requires Bryan's approval)

1. Do NOT create new `.astro` files or pages
2. Do NOT modify `BaseLayout.astro` or `PracticeLayout.astro` (layout/design files)
3. Do NOT change `wrangler.jsonc`, `astro.config.mjs`, or `package.json`
4. Do NOT add new npm dependencies
5. Do NOT change the design, colors, fonts, or styling
6. Do NOT restructure the project or change the tech stack
7. Do NOT delete any existing files
8. Do NOT deploy without Bryan's explicit permission
9. Do NOT touch any other Worker or project folder
10. Do NOT change any URL paths, redirects, or page structure (SEO protection)

## BLOG POST TEMPLATE

```markdown
---
title: "Post Title Here"
description: "One-sentence summary for SEO and blog listing."
pubDate: 2026-08-08
author: "Clifford Chigbu"
tags: ["family-law", "elk-grove"]
draft: false
---

Write the post content here in Markdown.
```

## BLOG TAGS (use 1-3 per post)

| Tag | Shows as category |
|-----|-------------------|
